# One customer's brand. Every variable is optional.
#
# Docker — one image, a brand per container:
#   docker run --env-file brands/example.env -e AGENT_URL=http://agent:3001 -p 8080:80 rafai-web
#
# Development, or a static build for Vercel/Netlify/S3 (written into
# dist/brand.js) — Vite reads .env.local in both:
#   cp brands/example.env .env.local && npm run dev        # or: npm run build
# On a hosting dashboard, set the same variables in its environment settings.
# Don't `source` this file: a shell runs `BRAND_NAME=Acme Assist` as a command.
#
# Leave a field unset and it falls back to this customer's own values, never to
# Rafai's: set only BRAND_NAME and the logo becomes a wordmark of the name and
# the tab icon a monogram of its first letter.
#
# Values
#   names    plain text
#   colours  6d28d9 or #6d28d9 — prefer no '#': in a .env file read by Vite an
#            unquoted '#' starts a comment and the value arrives EMPTY
#   images   /brands/<name>/<file> for a file in this repo's brands/ folder —
#            the build or the container copies in only the files named here —
#            or https://..., another /path on this site, or a data:image URL.
#            brands/cts/ is a complete set.

BRAND_NAME=Acme Assist
BRAND_COMPANY=Acme Logistics
BRAND_TAGLINE=Operations
# BRAND_LOGO_URL=/brands/acme/logo.png
# BRAND_LOGO_DARK_URL=/brands/acme/logo-dark.png
# BRAND_FAVICON_URL=/brands/acme/icon.png

# Buttons, links, tabs, focus rings, the question bubble. It is also used AS
# TEXT, so it must read at 4.5:1 — the build and the browser console warn if not.
BRAND_ACCENT=6d28d9
BRAND_ACCENT_DARK=a78bfa

# The 3px rule across the top. Defaults to the accent.
# BRAND_BAR=f59e0b

# The sidebar background. Its text colour is worked out from it.
BRAND_SIDEBAR=1e1b4b
# BRAND_SIDEBAR_DARK=0f0d2e
